# Prospective V2 renderer control declaration encoding

Actual author: `/root/research_architect`, before V2 generation. This NEW addendum clarifies the grouping ambiguity in the frozen V2 amendment's requirement that both sample IDs/renderers be bound. It changes no existing document, target, dynamics, property, source family, context or semantic pair requirement. No V1 decision may apply this new encoding retrospectively.

Use the already published exact version `rgm-planning-controls-2.0.0` and batch `planning-gap-v2`, with this addendum's actual hash bound before any dependent candidate/checker execution. `public_specification_bindings` now includes **seven** documents: `schemas/SEMANTICS.md`, `schemas/RGM_PLANNING_CONTROL_PROPERTIES.md`, `schemas/RGM_PLANNING_MANIFEST_ENCODING_SUPPLEMENT.md`, `research/curricula/RGM-NEXT-GAP-PROSPECTIVE.md`, `schemas/RGM_PLANNING_CONTROL_PROPERTIES_V2.md`, `research/curricula/RGM-PLANNING-GAP-V2-PROSPECTIVE.md`, and this addendum. The original six remain unchanged; missing/incorrect addendum binding is a future V2 interface failure, not authority to reinterpret an old manifest.

For **each required supplied semantic control pair**, each of the two actual renderer styles requires its own truthful control declaration in its family's existing `controls` list. A declaration's `sample_ids` contains exactly two distinct nonempty strings, ordered as the logical left/right intervention defined by the control. Both IDs must exist in the exact candidate, belong to the same source family/split, use the same renderer style, and occupy the declared two contexts. Verify actual parsed payload differences, obligations and evidence independently for each declaration. The two styles' declarations cover all four corresponding sample IDs. A single two-ID pair from only one style is insufficient for V2; a combined four-ID declaration does not satisfy this two-ID encoding. The context still binds its two rendered samples by the existing context interface.

The same `name` may and usually will occur more than once within a family's control list: once per renderer, and, if justified, for other actual supplied pairs. Never collapse that list to one control per name or infer uniqueness of name/pair/property. `control_id` must be a nonempty string **distinct for every declaration across this V2 manifest**; this is an explicit prospective custody requirement, not a historical or private evidence-ID convention. No exact ID format or spelling is required. Different truthful controls may reference the same sample pair, but use different control IDs and independently prove their named properties. There is no global uniqueness requirement for sample pairs or property names.

All original control fields remain: `control_id,name,scope="corpus_variant",sample_ids,changed_task_fields,provenance="supplied_tasks"`. Each C1 order declaration separately carries the V2 selective-clearance `evidence` with independently verified swap/failure indices, reason and six-guard truth object. Each C3/C4 append declaration separately carries `evidence` containing the exact prefix length, selected block and TABLE support. The facts may be equal across semantically equivalent styles, but the witness is still bound to each style's actual sample IDs. No extra closed shape, private expected field or unpublished row-witness-ID assumption is introduced.

The required supplied semantic controls total **96**: twelve fuel-only, twelve directed-edge deletion, twelve adjacent-order, twelve partial-goal extension, thirty-six valid goal-detour, and twelve isolated no-op append pairs. With two per-renderer declarations per semantic pair, the minimum complete layout contains **192 declarations**. These are renderer custody views of96 semantic controls, not192 independent interventions. Optional additional truthful controls must be reported separately and cannot replace a required pair or style.

The prospective data count remains408 correlated records /204 semantic inputs /48 revised source families (zero new family growth relative to pending V1). All original context/novelty/size/search/split gates and new V2 selective/C4 requirements remain mandatory. Decoder/producer/formal receipts must bind this addendum and their actual source versions before generation, reject mixed-style/missing-style/nonexistent-ID or false-field-difference declarations, and preserve first failures. A passing group count or matching annotation is not sufficient without exact per-style task/control evidence.

This public-only clarification responds to a formal integration question communicated by root. No formal private implementation, future candidate, gold or future review was read. The author designed V1/V2 and is separately adjudicating V1 after completed first reviews; common underlying-model and design/adjudicator overlap remain disclosed. This addendum generates or approves no candidate, target or release.
